= Physics bibliography

= Material Properties: OFHC Copper by National Institute of Standards and Technology
{c}
{parent=Physics bibliography}
{tag=Work by National Institute of Standards and Technology}

Official data and fitted coefficients: https://trc.nist.gov/cryogenics/materials/OFHC%20Copper/OFHC_Copper_rev1.htm

The specific-heat correlation covers 4–300 K and gives mass-specific <heat capacity> in $\mathrm{J\,kg^{-1}K^{-1}}$. Its stated fit deviation is 10% below 15 K. The page distinguishes specific heat from its separate <thermal conductivity> correlation.

= AN-1549: Performance Optimization of the Integrated ADC on the ADuCM4050 by Analog Devices
{parent=Physics bibliography}
{c}
{tag=Work by Analog Devices}
{title2=AN-1549}

Manufacturer application note. The <oversampling> and Averaging section discusses uncorrelated <noise> and <dither>; Table 1 gives fourfold sample-count increases per extra output bit. No individual author is established by the consulted HTML page.

https://www.analog.com/en/resources/app-notes/an-1549.html

= Introduction to Fourier Transform Spectroscopy by Julius Cohen
{parent=Physics bibliography}
{c}
{tag=Work by Julius Cohen}
{title2=1986; NBSIR 86-3339}

Institutional report on the <Michelson interferometer>, interferograms, <Fourier transform spectroscopy>, <interferogram apodization>, resolution and sampling. Chapters 13–16 derive the reconstruction and discuss finite-window and sampling limitations.

https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/Legacy/IR/nbsir86-3339.pdf

= LM741 Operational Amplifier by Texas Instruments
{parent=Physics bibliography}
{c}
{tag=Work by Texas Instruments}
{title2=SNOSC25D}
{title2=2015}

Manufacturer's data sheet, revision D, October 2015.

https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/lm741.pdf

Section 6.5, p. 5, gives typical <input impedance> $2\,\mathrm{M\Omega}$ at $25^\circ\mathrm C$ and typical large-signal <voltage gain> $200\,\mathrm{V/mV}$. Section 7.4.2 describes closed-loop feedback. These are device-specific examples for interpreting a real <operational amplifier>.

= Position Space Renormalization Group by Mehran Kardar
{c}
{parent=Physics bibliography}
{tag=Work by Mehran Kardar}

Author-hosted MIT course notes: https://web.mit.edu/8.334/www/lectures/lec13.pdf[Lecture 13, printed pp. 75–81] and https://web.mit.edu/8.334/www/lectures/lec14.pdf[Lecture 14, printed pp. 82–88]. No revision date is inferred from the host's current course navigation.

Lecture 13, section V.B, equations V.13–V.27 develops exact one-dimensional <spin decimation>, its normalization and scaling variables. Lecture 14, section V.D, printed pp. 86–87, equations V.51–V.54 specifies <bond moving> followed by chain decimation. The official MIT 8.334 course page identifies <Mehran Kardar> as instructor.

= Driven coherent oscillations of a single electron spin in a quantum dot by F. H. L. Koppens and others
{parent=Physics bibliography}
{tag=Work by F. H. L. Koppens}
{c}
