= Electron-electron interactions in antidot-based Aharonov-Bohm interferometers by S. Ihnatsenka and others
{c}
{parent=Physics bibliography}
{tag=Work by S. Ihnatsenka}
{title2=2009}
{title2=10.1103/PhysRevB.80.115303}

Physical Review B 80, 115303. https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.80.115303

Primary preprint: https://arxiv.org/abs/0905.1338

Section I discusses edge-channel connectivity and the distinction between fixed-area <flux> counting and charging-modified <periods>. Section III.C, Fig. 7, discusses scattering-induced transmission via antidot-bound states. The calculation treats interaction effects and should not be read as a universal prediction of isolated Lorentzian peaks.

= Single-shot readout of electron spin states in a quantum dot using spin-dependent tunnel rates by R. Hanson and others
{c}
{parent=Physics bibliography}
{tag=Work by R. Hanson}
{title2=2005}
{title2=10.1103/PhysRevLett.94.196802}

Physical Review Letters 94, 196802. https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.94.196802

Primary preprint, submitted 31 December 2004: https://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/0412768

Pages 1–2 describe energy-selective versus tunnel-rate-selective conversion and the two-electron orbital mechanism. Figures 1–2 show timing/readout; Fig. 4 examines nearly degenerate states. The 2004 preprint date differs from the 2005 journal year.

