https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.87.012008

= Numerical Calculations of the Dynamics of a Collapsing Proto-Star by Richard B. Larson
{parent=Physics bibliography}
{c}
{tag=Work by Richard B. Larson}
{title2=1969}
{title2=Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society 145, 271–295}

The primary numerical study follows spherical protostellar collapse. A small central core forms before most of the envelope reaches it and subsequently grows by <accretion>. The abstract also describes infrared reprocessing by the dusty envelope. Spherical symmetry and the chosen radiative and thermodynamic treatment are model assumptions; rotation, <magnetic fields> and non-spherical <accretion> require additional physics.

https://academic.oup.com/mnras/article/145/3/271/2602795

https://doi.org/10.1093/mnras/145.3.271

= The Neutral Atomic Phases of the ISM in the Galaxy by Mark G. Wolfire and others
{parent=Physics bibliography}
{c}
{tag=Work by Mark G. Wolfire}
{title2=2003}
{title2=The Astrophysical Journal 587, 278–311}

The primary model computes cold and warm atomic equilibrium branches and the <pressure> interval where they coexist. Its heating and cooling depend on the radiation field, <ionization> and gas abundances. This is a thermal-phase model for the Milky Way disk, not a claim that all interstellar phases share one <pressure> or a perfectly static configuration.

https://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/0207098

https://doi.org/10.1086/368016

= Criterion for Ferromagnetism from Observations of Magnetic Isotherms by Anthony Arrott
{c}
{parent=Physics bibliography}
{tag=Work by Anthony Arrott}

Physical Review 108, 1394 (1957), published 15 December 1957.

https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRev.108.1394

Primary publisher abstract: within a molecular-field description, the onset criterion follows from magnetisation cubed being proportional to internal field at the Curie point. This source supports the named plotting method, not the numerical estimates independently read from an exam graph.

