Its <potassium-40> decay scheme gives the approximate atomic mass-energy differences of $1.311$ MeV to <calcium-40> and $1.505$ MeV to <argon-40>, and distinguishes capture to an excited argon level from the rare positron branch. The positron kinetic-energy endpoint additionally subtracts $2m_e$ from the atomic mass difference.

